In article <CsHKMK.75s@oci.utoronto.ca>, jae@apollo.stanford.edu (Jae K. Kim) writes:
>I am playing a game in which I cannot find the down staircase in the first
>maze i.e. around level 23.  Basically, the question that I have is: 
>
>how the hell do I find the staircase?!
>
>I've tried using the wand of wishing to make one, but it fails.  I've tried
>magic mapping, but it doesn't appear.  I'm getting desperate.  Could someone
>out there send me some illuminating email about this matter?

Sounds like you're playing a fairly old version.  I was stuck at that 
spot in that version *forever*.  I tried everything I could think of
(including trying to polymorph traps to turn them into trap door which 
I could go through).  In old versions, once you get to the maze, there 
are no down stairs, only upstairs.  The way to get down to where the
wizard is to:
























get fire resistance, and teleport control.  Become confused and then read
a scroll of teleportation.  When confused, this acts as a level teleporter.
With teleport control, it will ask you which level you want to teleport
to.  Respond 50, and then start at level 50 and make your way up until you
find the Wizard.  Kill him, take the amulet, and keep going up to the 
entrance on level 1.
